# Q2: 103, 101, 197, 151, 127, 137, 179, 199, 191, 109

**Basic statistics:**
- Count: 10 numbers
- Sum: 1,494
- Mean: 149.4
- Range: 101 to 199
- All odd numbers

**Interesting observation:** Every number is **odd**, and checking primality:

- 103 — prime
- 101 — prime
- 197 — prime
- 151 — prime
- 127 — prime
- 137 — prime
- 179 — prime
- 199 — prime
- 191 — prime
- 109 — prime

**All ten numbers are prime!** They're all odd primes between 100 and 200. Specifically, these are 10 of the 21 primes in that range (the full list being 101, 103, 107, 109, 113, 127, 131, 137, 139, 149, 151, 157, 163, 167, 173, 179, 181, 191, 193, 197, 199).

**Bonus observation:** All of these primes are of the form... let me check mod 4: 103≡3, 101≡1, 197≡1, 151≡3, 127≡3, 137≡1, 179≡3, 199≡3, 191≡3, 109≡1. Mixed 1 and 3 mod 4 — no pattern there.

The most striking fact is simply: **all ten are primes between 100 and 200**. [end of text]


